USB HID builder portions in src/bin/products/rp_usb_fido_common.rs and
src/bin/products/trustzone/tz_nonsecure.rs follow the Embassy RP HID example,
examples/rp/src/bin/usb_hid_mouse.rs. Comparison snapshot:
0af1937a5ac77f52fea943b677088c38ef9e91c6, embassy-rs/embassy.
Copyright (c) Embassy project contributors. Original portions retain
MIT OR Apache-2.0 under root vendor/cyw43-portable/LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE.
Changes include static buffers, CTAPHID identity/report configuration,
dispatcher/gateway integration and separate frontend tasks.
The comparison snapshot does not identify the exact historical borrowing revision.

The same USB HID builder attribution applies to the retained builder branch in
src/bin/products/trustzone/tz_nonsecure_usb_ble.rs. Its gateway, ingress arbiter,
bond conversion and transport-task integration are ManeKey changes; included
shared BLE and USB implementations retain their separate original terms.

CYW43 initialization and advertising in
src/bin/products/ble/pico_cyw43_ble_common.rs and
src/bin/products/ble/riscv_pico_2_w_ble_common.rs and
src/bin/products/pmp/pmp_ble_user_image.rs follow TrouBLE examples.
Comparison snapshot: b6043f576b482d8a4ecd7d2634df48cba20bd7ba,
embassy-rs/trouble, examples/rp-pico-w/src/bin/ble_bas_peripheral.rs and
examples/apps/src/ble_bas_peripheral.rs.
Copyright (c) Embassy project contributors. Original portions retain
MIT OR Apache-2.0 under root vendor/cyw43-portable/LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE.
Changes include FIDO services, shared ingress, stored bonds, notification
handling and selectable PIO transport. The snapshot is a comparison reference,
not a claim identifying the exact historical borrowing revision.
The RISC-V variant changes HAL ownership, polling PIO setup, runtime selection
and shared USB/Internal ingress; its PIO program retains the separate terms below.
The split PMP user image changes descriptor-backed SPI, checked ecalls,
shared ingress and monitor-owned timer handling. Its queue scheduling also
follows Embassy embassy-rp/src/time_driver.rs at comparison snapshot
0af1937a5ac77f52fea943b677088c38ef9e91c6, retaining the same included
MIT OR Apache-2.0 terms and Embassy contributor attribution.

Public source distributions do not include the NVRAM binary. Set
MANEKEY_CYW43_NVRAM_FILE to an explicitly obtained file from
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/embassy-rs/embassy/0af1937a5ac77f52fea943b677088c38ef9e91c6/cyw43-firmware/nvram_rp2040.bin
The build verifies 742 bytes and SHA-256
4904bdbb0c937bd0ac2eb2a1d62f2da4dd90e32082384e02874e8d671b0f330d.
No automatic download or additional redistribution permission is granted.

The NVRAM originates from the binary distributed by
Embassy at revision 0af1937a5ac77f52fea943b677088c38ef9e91c6.
Its upstream license text is included at
assets/cyw43/LICENSE-permissive-binary-license-1.0.txt.
The ManeKey port license does not replace that binary's terms.

